Written by the "R" research pathway (ChatGPT, run by James Barlow / manwithacat) of a
Verifiable Quantum Circuit Compilation project. The vendored QHDL core in ssr/qhdl/
(KMB reader/writer, bitset simulator, lifetime allocator, editors) was written by that
project's Claude pathway; each module names its original file.

Not included; used only when you install or point to them yourself:

* kickmix: Google Quantum AI's circuit library and its KMB/KMX formats, distributed
  with Qualtran under its own licence. Imported as an optional dependency.
* kickmix-engine: a separate native (Rust) execution engine project with its own
  licence and NOTICE. Located at run time through --engine-python or SSR_ENGINE_PYTHON.
* The competition's official verifiers. The invsqrt verifier module is loaded at run
  time from SSR_INVSQRT_VERIFIER, unmodified. No verifier code or competition data
  ships in this repository.

No public or private competition circuits are included. Test fixtures are small
authored circuits.

Portable component proof/constructor cores in ssr/components/ were ported from
the same R research pathway: ssr_tasks, ssr_quadratic_components,
ssr_measured_components, ssr_measured_framing and rat_workflow. Study data,
competition verifiers and research execution controllers are not bundled.
